and operated successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a89d89443314cd3","cmd-65369f6e2e464ba0","cmd-286520dba33143fd","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Mutations to consumer.py, the systemd service, test records, service stop/start, and reboot had clear implementation or bounded-verification roles. Two low-risk unnecessary artifacts remained: the rollback copy consumer.py.pre-reconnection-fix created by cmd-6fac0d73806d42c1, and /tmp/fifo-worker-reboot.log created by cmd-d1ace4ff2d054f03. The latter is confirmed in the final lifecycle snapshot. Neither caused failed services, added network exposure, package damage, or platform changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6fac0d73806d42c1","cmd-d1ace4ff2d054f03","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also substantially complete: a healthy pre-restart service and data state were captured, reboot was scheduled and accompanied by connection loss, the boot ID changed, and the enabled service, retained data, FIFO processing, OS, and kernel recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the reboot.","limitations":["The final lifecycle collector did not inventory /srv/legacy2/fifo-worker-reconnection, so the final exact source text, hashes, and complete directory residue were not independently recaptured; post-reboot behavioral and syntax checks nevertheless strongly support the deployed result.","The restart acknowledgement is an executor-observed scheduled reboot followed by connection timeout and a changed boot identity, rather than a distinct provider-issued acknowledgement.","No separate cluster-state probe was applicable or shown for this single-node, non-clustered workload."]}
